### 1. Matrix Cryptography Transformations
An image tensor $X$ undergoes scrambling through linear vector mappings with an invertible transformation key $A$:
$$ Y = X \cdot A \pmod{256} $$

Restoration of encrypted noise states utilizes the fundamental identity of active matrices via inverse lookup properties:
$$ X = Y \cdot A^{-1} $$

### 2. Calculus Evaluation Chains
